{
  "comment": "Named DROP curves, shared by every mob. A mob def doesn't spell out its own odds — it names a curve per droppable in its `lootTable` block (e.g. \"rock_petal\": \"normal-high\"), so retuning how generous 'normal-high' is retunes every mob that uses it at once. Each curve is keyed by the MOB'S rarity, and each of those is a list of OUTCOMES: one roll picks exactly one entry, and that entry says what you get. `chance` is read as a percentage but rolled against the list's own sum, so a set that doesn't total 100 still behaves sensibly. `count` is how many drop (0 = nothing, and the usual first entry). `rarity` is what rarity they drop AT — omit it and the drop matches the mob's own rarity, which is why most entries here don't need it. A LIST, not an object keyed by chance, because two outcomes can legitimately share a percentage and duplicate JSON keys would silently collapse. `default` covers any rarity a curve doesn't list, which keeps these files short as rarity tiers get added.",

